From: Agent
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: SPL: when booted from MMC2, register only the eMMC slot

With CONFIG_SPL_MMC_TINY there is a single static struct mmc, so the
"MMC2 -> device index 1" lookup in spl_mmc.c ends up initialising whichever
slot was registered. With CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA=-1 only slot 0 (empty
SD socket) is registered and the SPL fails with
"Card did not respond to voltage select! : -110".

Registering both slots at once was reported to brown out the board, so when
the BROM booted us from MMC2, bring up only the extra (eMMC) slot.

---
 board/sunxi/board.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -510,6 +510,18 @@

 int board_mmc_init(struct bd_info *bis)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_XPL_BUILD
+	/*
+	 * Booted from the eMMC: bring up only that slot, avoiding the dual
+	 * initialisation and making it the one the SPL MMC code finds.
+	 */
+	if (CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA != -1 &&
+	    sunxi_get_boot_device() == BOOT_DEVICE_MMC2) {
+		mmc_pinmux_setup(CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA);
+		return sunxi_mmc_init(CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA) ? 0 : -1;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	/*
 	 * The BROM always accesses MMC port 0 (typically an SD card), and
 	 * most boards seem to have such a slot. The others haven't reported
